{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1412776-gods-manifesting-in-the-world","id":1412776,"title":"Gods manifesting in the World","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-09-09T17:56:23-07:00","id":1412776,"title":"Gods manifesting in the World","content":"I start reading about the god realms and start to questioning how the gods manifest in the world.<br /> <br /> The \u201cstandard\u201d Gods just pop in the world with many powers is pretty much the way the Theoi shows up in their myths, while capable of look like any person, animal or even concept, they can also be present in the local they want without being seen, maybe shapeshifting into air, or what ever.<br /> <br /> That is basically how the gods are portrayed in 1e, and I think it\u2019s not the case on all myths. Well, I am almost sure it\u2019s not the case.<br /> For example, the Orisha don\u2019t manifest in the world, they usually use worshipers or mediums bodies to do so.<br /> I am almost sure the Netjer have the same rules, they don\u2019t manifest in the world, only in Maat, requiring a body (or object) to be present in the world (they can perceive the world from the Maat, but have some limits).<br /> The way the Bogovi were described, it looks like they don\u2019t manifest in the world at full power, \u201conly in the 3x10th Kindom you will be elbow to elbow with a god\u201d.<br /> <br /> Do you guys think it will be discussed in God? Do you think it\u2019s even relevant?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurp